in @code

in @code/metalogue

in @prism

in @glass

in @meta

in @nl

in @property

# @code/rust/macro — the Rust altitude's metalogue realisation.
#
# The 34th-instance recognition (2026-06-09, Reed + Alex → Mara):
# "macro" is the language-community word; `@code/metalogue` is the
# substrate word. This file is the Rust-altitude realisation of
# `@code/metalogue` — the universal contract lives at the ground
# (shards/code/metalogue.mirror), this shard binds it to Rust's
# proc-macro surface (`#[proc_macro]`, `#[proc_macro_derive]`,
# `#[proc_macro_attribute]`) and to Rust's typed AST
# (`code/rust.ast`). The name "macro" stays at the species altitude
# because that's the community vocabulary Rust users recognize; the
# substrate gains `@code/metalogue` as the universal ground via the
# `in @code/metalogue` inheritance above.
#
# Why under `@code/rust` (not a new `@code/macro` family): per
# docs/specs/code-metalogue-surface.md §2 substrate-pull check,
# `@code` is the universal grammar-at-altitude discipline, and
# `@code/X` species carry per-language altitude grammars. The
# metalogue/macro reception sub-prism IS-A part of the language
# altitude (the way `@code/rust/cargo` IS-A part of `@code/rust`),
# not a sibling family. Path-namespace property per
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]: this file at
# `shards/code/rust/macro.mirror` declares `@code/rust/macro`. The
# path IS the declaration.
#
# === Inheritance from @code/metalogue (the universal ground) ===
#
# The four-shim contract (`shim_type`, `shim_prism`, `shim_action`,
# `shim_grammar`), the four laws (round-trip, oid-functionality,
# type-soundness, substrate-pull preservation), and the
# declaration/turn/metalogue_session carrier types are declared
# ONCE at `shards/code/metalogue.mirror`. This shard inherits them
# via `in @code/metalogue` per
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]'s `<=` mechanism
# (`in @X` is the canonical import-and-inherit form). The shim
# signatures below specialize the ground's parametric
# `species_ast` to Rust's `code/rust.ast`; the laws come for free
# from the ground's `requires` clauses.
#
# === The smallest tick (the T23-T26 cascade) ===
#
# Per docs/specs/code-metalogue-surface.md §12 "Implementation
# cascade — the smallest tick that proves the shape":
#
#   T23 (landed) — `shim_type` for the simplest substrate-
#     declaration kind (the `type` kind) end-to-end through
#     `prism/derive/src/declaration.rs`'s `declaration!`
#     proc-macro plus four round-trip OID tests.
#   T24 (landing) — `shim_prism` for the bare `prism @path`
#     declaration form. The three RED tests at
#     `prism/core/tests/declaration_round_trip.rs` discharge
#     against this binding.
#   T25 — `shim_action` (forward-promised; consumer-pulls at
#     `kintsugi-on-Rust` T22+).
#   T26 — `shim_grammar` (forward-promised).
#
# === Spec context ===
#
# docs/specs/code-metalogue-surface.md §4 (typed surface at the
# ground), §4.1 (four kinds dispatch), §5 (the four laws
# formalized at the ground), §6 (round-trip identity — the central
# contract), §10.1 (the dispatch table at the ground), §11 (the
# per-species matrix — this shard is the canonical row), §12 (the
# cascade).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]],
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]].
# Related shards: code/metalogue.mirror (the universal ground —
# declares the contract and laws), code.mirror (universal parent),
# code/rust.mirror (the Rust altitude the sub-prism specialises),
# code/mirror.mirror (T17 — the render half at the mirror altitude;
# the sibling-altitude precedent for the round-trip law).

prism @code/rust/macro {
  focus macro
  project macro
  split macro
  shift macro
  settle macro
}

# === Rust-altitude shim bindings ===
#
# The four shim signatures from `@code/metalogue` (universal
# contract) bind here to `code/rust.ast` as the species AST type.
# The contract and laws inherit from the ground via
# `in @code/metalogue`; this shard's job is the per-altitude
# binding plus the realisation cascade (T23 type ✓, T24 prism
# landing, T25 action forward, T26 grammar forward).
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]: bodies are `\` until a
# consumer-pull tick. The Rust proc-macro at
# `prism/derive/src/declaration.rs` IS the consumer; the laws
# discharge through the round-trip OID tests at
# `prism/core/tests/declaration_round_trip.rs`.

shim_type(d: declaration) -> code/rust.ast { \ }
shim_prism(d: declaration) -> code/rust.ast { \ }
shim_action(d: declaration) -> code/rust.ast { \ }
shim_grammar(d: declaration) -> code/rust.ast { \ }

# === project_hole binding — Rust's explicit lossy projection ===
#
# The 35th-instance recognition (2026-06-09, Alex → Mara via Reed):
# during T25 GREEN the substrate's `\` could not survive Rust source
# at the proc-macro call site. Two altitudes need explicit naming
# because Rust's surface and Rust's AST realise the hole differently:
#
#   - Source-text altitude (call site):   substrate `\`  ↔ Rust `{ }`
#       the empty block is the Rust-lexer-realisable surface form at
#       proc-macro call sites. The proc-macro receives a TokenStream
#       containing the `{ }` braces; this IS the surface-level
#       projection of the hole the Rust lexer admits.
#
#   - AST altitude (emission body):       substrate `\`  ↔ `todo!()`
#       the Rust stdlib's `todo!` macro expands to an
#       `unimplemented!`-shaped runtime panic. The proc-macro emits
#       `todo!()` as the body for any action whose substrate `\` body
#       was not resolved (consumer-pull deferred per
#       [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]). `todo!()` is close to a
#       typed-gap (it has type `!`, the never type, which unifies
#       with any expected return type — closer to substrate-hole
#       semantics than `unimplemented!()` or `panic!()`); it is the
#       least-lossy projection Rust admits.
#
# Per Alex's read: *"No language has the exact semantics of the
# hole. It will always be a projection."* Rust's `todo!()` is the
# closest typed-gap available; `_` is a wildcard not an action body;
# `{ }` is an empty unit-returning block. None match the substrate
# hole exactly. The lossy delta is admitted at the @glass altitude
# as transparency on the metalogue turn that carries this projection.
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]: the substrate
# already had `hole`; this shard names Rust's lossy projection of
# `hole` rather than inventing a new substrate noun. The naming
# "lexical glass-wall" (Mara's initial candidate during T25) is
# rejected per the substrate-pull-correct framing: the carrier IS
# `hole`, the operation IS `project`, the per-species explicit
# mapping IS `project_hole`'s body at this altitude.
#
# Per the metalogue ground (shards/code/metalogue.mirror lines 245+),
# `project_hole` is the universal contract; this shard's job is the
# Rust-altitude binding. The body stays `\` until the consumer-pull
# tick that needs the typed projection (T25+ for `shim_action`'s
# round-trip law to discharge through `todo!()` rather than ad-hoc
# emission).

project_hole(h: hole) -> code/rust.ast { \ }

out @code/rust/macro
out shim_type
out shim_prism
out shim_action
out shim_grammar
out project_hole
